Path planner field backdrops

    The perimeter arrangements drawn in web/src/lib/field.ts and PathSim.tsx —
    square, square with inverted alliance areas, and diamond — are our own line
    drawings of geometry the FTC Docs state in the *FIRST* Tech Challenge Field
    Coordinate System Definition: origin at the centre of the field, 6x6 tiles
    of 24 inches, 3580mm between the inside faces of the perimeter panels.

    The DECODE 2025-2026 tape layout in web/src/lib/field.ts is transcribed from
    section 8, "Initial Tape Installation", of the 2025-2026 *FIRST* Tech
    Challenge Event FIELD Setup Guide — the written placements and the numbers
    they give (10in SPIKE MARKS and GATE ZONE segments, 18in BASE ZONE squares,
    SECRET TUNNEL lines 16.75in inside seam V or Z). The guide places tape
    against the TILE grid, so the grid is what the code follows.

    No FIRST field rendering is used, traced or reproduced, and no other
    season's tape layout is drawn. Those are not in the index, and a planner that draws tape in
    the wrong place is worse than one that draws none. A team that wants a
    specific season's field supplies its own image, which is read in the browser
    and never uploaded.
